{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794819226,"nonce":"SccpznWGcscR4WUQLfWPYqswFWQ=","title":"Rows move every stream a batch draws, with one clip model","message":"Part of the GPU-deferral plan (da827f7). Root causes behind this week's rows regressions and declines on the cn_demo page, found by looking at the engine rather than at components.\n\n1. Rows move only primitives. A paint batch also holds ordered images (drawn through the paint context inside cross-stream groups), tessellated path vertices, glass, meshes, GPU passes and layer commands, none of which carry a node slot. NodeRows::plan declines the whole batch if any is present, so one image in a faded group puts a whole scrolled page on full paints. SVGs, canvases, stacks and ordered images were all this rule.\n\n2. Clips are computed by several models that disagree: the GPU paint walk (one rect plus one shape per primitive), the element collection walk (images: primary plus scroll clip; SVGs and text: one intersected rect, now split for moved content), canvas replay and paths with their own. All were built for full paints, where intersecting into screen space is harmless; rows need the part that stays (the viewport) apart from the part that moves, and each model loses it differently, so each rows fix has to be made three or four times.\n\nTarget: every drawable a batch holds carries a slot and one clip form (a clip rect that stays, plus a shape that follows the rows from a depth), so plan() declines only what truly cannot move.\n\nSteps, each its own issue:\n- ordered images take slots and follow the rows (blocks the cn_demo page: 2abee0a)\n- one clip form shared by primitives, dynamic images, images, SVGs, glyphs and canvas replay\n- path vertices and layer-command groups take slots\n- lift the stack / nested-scroll guard and put 'scroll a page with clips of its own' and 'scroll grouped images, then stop' in ON_ROWS\n\nRelated: c3080f6 (per-frame cost once moved content is the whole page), 660c14b (text shape pointers compared across aux spaces), 2abee0a (image list lost after a decline).\n\ngit-bug: da827f735d1c968d08fe95d9c181ee4436346ddc1692e2081ab253c339e57afe","files":null}]}